## 3. "GEM CHEF CUISTOT" & CULINARY LAWS (POWERED BY GEMINI PRO)

### The Double Declination & Appliances
- Base recipe must be shared (seasonal veggies, carbs, spices).
- Alexis: Vegan protein (tofu, legumes). Élodie: Animal or alternative protein.
- Appliances: Recipes MUST optimize KitchenAid (explicit cut type: râpé fin / lamelles), Thermomix (exact speed/time **only if actually blending**), Cookeo, **cuiseur à riz** (rice — never boil rice / never Cookeo for rice), Airfryer (time + °C; vegan/omnivore proteins same basket when possible), Oven, and Stove.
- Galette / naan / pain / wrap / pita / tortilla: pan or oven. NEVER water-cook.
- Persona: expert chef, densité S34. NEVER bland bowls. Almost every meal includes fresh herbs (mint, basil, parsley, chives — NEVER coriander), spices (cumin, paprika, 5-spice, ginger), and a **homemade** sauce/marinade (tahini, soy, ginger, citrus). Generation MUST read `lib/kitchen-prefs.ts` (Paramètres foyer).
- **Sauces 100% maison** (`lib/homemade-sauces.ts`): NEVER a single jar line (« Sauce satay 40g », pesto du commerce) with components only in notes. Explode satay / houmous / pesto / pistou / nuoc / vinaigrette / sauce tahini-citron into separate ingredient rows, each with grams + `visual_unit` (cc / cs / gousse / cm / pièce), plus a mix step. Satay = beurre de sésame (NEVER peanut butter). Present the group in the recipe UI like any other sauce (`lib/ingredient-groups.ts` label « Sauce satay », « Vinaigrette », …).

### Cooking & Batchcooking Constraints
- TOFU — weekday batchcooking (Mon–Fri): tofu is NEVER cooked during the main batch session. It is pressed, marinated, chilled, and served fresh at plating.
- TOFU — EXCEPTIONS (cooking allowed): (1) desserts / baking; (2) weekend recipes.
- MOCK MEATS — weekday batch: do not cook simili-carné (vegan steaks, vegan sausages, etc.) during the Mon–Fri session.
- WEEKEND RULE: mock meats (simili-carné: vegan steaks, vegan sausages, etc.) AND cooked tofu are fully allowed.
- UI / PDF copy: positive, actionable steps only (what TO DO). Do NOT add redundant “do not cook tofu” warnings in step descriptions when tofu is not being cooked in that step. Warnings = real hazards (aversions), not tofu slogans.
- 2-PORTION RULE (weekdays): every generated weekday batch recipe covers EXACTLY 2 MEALS per person (batch of 10 meals = 5 recipes × 2).
- 1-PORTION RULE (weekend): every weekend recipe is 1 fresh meal per person (batch of 4 meals: Sat lunch, Sat dinner, Sun lunch, Sun dinner). No double-batch.
- LOW CALORIE DINNER: all evening meals must strictly be "Low Calorie" variants.
- WEATHER RULE: adapt recipes to weather (e.g., Bowls/Bo Bun/Salads during heatwaves).

### Meal generation & control logic (Tab 3 · Gem Chef · Gemini Pro)
- NEVER generate a full week in one undifferentiated dump. Granular controls only:
  1. **Generate Mon–Fri** — 5 batch recipes covering 10 meals, 2-meal portion rule. Pairings ALTERNATE days (never consecutive): Lun+Mer déjeuner, Mar+Jeu déjeuner, Lun+Mer dîner (low cal), Mar+Jeu dîner (low cal), Ven déjeuner+Ven dîner (same base, dinner plated lighter).
  2. **Generate Weekend** — 4 fresh meals, 1-meal portion rule (Sat/Sun lunch + dinner).
  3. **Generate / regenerate a single meal** (or its weekday batch pair).
  4. **Theme** — a theme text field is applied BEFORE every generation (preset or custom: Tomate, Italien, Asiatique, Bowl, Épicé, etc.). The theme ingredient/family MUST be the central star of every generated recipe (title + shared base + major ingredient + a dedicated step), never a cosmetic subtitle.
- Week navigation: previous / today / next week. Missing weeks are EMPTY by default (no seed / auto-generation). « Vider la semaine » deletes all meals for the selected week. Each meal card has **Supprimer** (weekday batch = both pair slots) and **Déplacer** (pick day + déjeuner/dîner, swap slot contents, persist immediately). Each week is stored in Supabase `plans_semaine` (`week_start` = Monday). Fallback: localStorage if Supabase is unavailable.
- **AI memory:** generation fetches unique meal titles from the last 4 weeks and passes `past_meals` to Gemini: never repeat those titles. **Also merge** the household **Plus jamais** list (`lib/rejected.ts` `mergeAvoidTitles`) — those titles are forbidden until the user removes them, not only for 4 weeks. Today-swap uses the same avoid list.
- **Smart Guided Swap:** user picks WHICH ingredient to replace. Gemini Pro must suggest EXACTLY 3 culinary-coherent alternatives BEFORE any regeneration. User picks one; the whole recipe (and its weekday batch pair) is re-adapted. NEVER a free-text replacement field.
- API: `POST /api/generate-meals` (Gemini Pro). Modes: `weekdays` | `weekend` | `single` | `suggest-swap` | `apply-swap` | `today-swap` (Aujourd'hui Remplacement, 1 repas du jour, ne touche pas `plans_semaine`). Strict JSON: `title`, ingredients with `grams_alexis` / `grams_elodie` (same dish, per-profile portions from `lib/meal-coach.ts`) or `weight_g` + **`visual_unit`** (fresh produce: `"2 pièces"`, `"1/2 botte"`; sauces/spices: `"1 cs"` / `"1 cc"`; also accept `visual_quantity`), `prep`, `step_groups` in **up to 4 categories** (1 Cuissons Airfryer parallel vegan/omni → 2 Cuissons Eau / Plaques → 3 Thermomix sauces with `15 sec / V6` → 4 Découpes KitchenAid & Assemblage with `râpé fin` / `lamelles`). **Omit an empty group** (no TM if a jar whisk is enough; no Airfryer if nothing cooks). Water times are **per ingredient** (haricots verts 8 min ≠ pommes de terre 18 min); NEVER one shared « 8 min » on a mixed line. Herbs (thym, menthe…) never get their own water line. `tips_and_cautions` (batch logistics ONLY, never aversions / « sans X »). Theme, if set, must be creative and prominent — never a garnish. Unique meals are tagged `[P1]`, `[P2]`… (`components/repas/RecipeTag.tsx` + `lib/plan-colors.ts`) — **same colors** on Semaine, Courses, Batch. Display format: `Tomates cerises : 2 pièces (250g)` and `Tomates cerises : 6 pièces (840g) - [P1, P3]`. Recipe sheet: sticky close, compact one-line ingredients, **HoldTip** on truncated text, qty toggle repas vs total à cuisiner (`lib/qty-scale.ts`). If the key is missing, fall back to the local catalog (mock) rather than crashing.

### Interactive shopping list (Tab 3)
- Derived from the **current week's plan** (the week selected in the week navigator) via `lib/shopping-from-plan.ts`.
- Checkable items, grouped by supermarket aisle (FRUITS & LÉGUMES, FRAIS / RAYON BIO, VIANDES & POISSONS, BOULANGERIE, ÉPICERIE SALÉE, ÉPICES & CONDIMENTS, SURGELÉS, AUTRE). Aisle **dot + header colors** match recipe ingredient dots (`lib/plan-colors.ts`; Tailwind must scan `./lib/**`).
- **Buyable product, not prep / dish name.** Merge lines by canonical name (`shoppingDisplayName`): `Carotte julienne` + `Carotte râpée` + `Carotte` → one **Carotte** with **summed pièces + grams** and **all** recipe tags (P1, P2, P3, P5). `Tofu ferme mariné` → **Tofu ferme** (keep **Tofu soyeux** / fumé separate). `Poulet Yassa` / `Poulet paprika` → **Poulet**. Drop julienne, râpé, mariné, yassa, dish names from the shopping line. Recipe cards keep the prep.
- **Eau** is never listed (`isUnlistedShoppingIng`).
- **Bœuf** and **Œufs** go to VIANDES & POISSONS (normalize `œ` → `oe` in aisle matching). Sauce soja stays a grocery condiment; « sauce satay » does not — it has been exploded into tahini / soja / citron / etc.
- User can add custom items manually (they persist with the list for that week).
- Compact row: checkbox + aisle dot + truncated text + compact P-tags. **HoldTip** (hover / long-press) shows the full line; long-press must NOT toggle the checkbox.
- **"Copy for Apple Notes"** = plain text only: aisle headers, then `Name : Visual Unit (Weightg) - [P1, P3]` lines. NO checkboxes, NO bullet points, NO Markdown formatting.
- Unique recipe tags `[P1]`… appear on grocery lines so each item is tied to the résumé meals.

### Batchcooking Master Plan & PDF export (Tab 3)
- Built from the week's weekday batches (2 meals/person) + weekend fresh meals (1 each). Same data powers the on-screen déroulé AND the PDF.
- DÉROULÉ cards (UI + PDF) must be actionable. For every step / appliance instruction, EXPLICITLY list:
  - Exact ingredient names and quantities (batch qty = per-meal grams × servings; show profile when the ingredient is Alexis-only or Élodie-only, e.g. `Tofu ferme mariné : 1/2 bloc (320g) · Alexis`).
  - The associated recipe number/title (e.g. `Pour Recette #2: Bowl riz satay`).
  - Exact appliance parameters: temperature, mode, and cooking time (e.g. `200°C chaleur tournante · 25 min`, `Cuiseur à riz`, `Airfryer 180°C · 18 min`).
- **Eau / féculents:** one line per ingredient with **its own** time. Do not apply a shared « 8 min » to mixed veg. Potatoes ~18 min, green beans ~8 min. Herbs never a solo water line (attach to a companion cook, or sauce / assembly). Galette / naan / pain / wrap: never in this section.
- **Thermomix:** homemade sauces with **dosed** components (same exploded list as the recipe). Rinse the bowl between sauces.
- **Assemblage / packing (`lib/batch-from-plan.ts` + `lib/s34-copy.ts`):** merge Composition + Montage into **Boîte Alexis / Boîte Élodie** + **Pot sauce · à part**. Quantities = **1 box = 1 meal**; weekday copy **« 1 repas / boîte · à faire ×2 »**. Sauce classification is **name-only** (`isPotSauceIng` / `isSolidBoxFood`) — notes like « mariné soja » / « à l’eau » must NOT send tofu, edamame or veg to the pot. Shared split portions: leave `who` unset (never `who: "Alexis / Élodie"`, which `groupedCellIngredients` ignores and shows as empty **Ingrédient —**). Couple UI / batch / PDF show `grams_alexis` vs `grams_elodie` when they differ.
- Number unique recipes `[P1]`… (weekdays then weekend). UI résumé + daily cards + PDF + shopping use the **same colored tags**.
- DÉROULÉ / mise en place ingredient lines: `Tomates cerises : 6 pièces (840g) - [P1]` (name : visual unit (weight) + tag).
- Callouts stay: Tips / Warnings / Storage. Warnings are aversions and real hazards only.
- Export: PDF style **S34** — condensé et lisible. Pages 1–2 = déroulé master (1 Airfryer protéines en lignes ` [P1] : … ➔ 8 min`, 2 féculents **une durée / ingrédient**, 3 table Thermomix Plat / Ingrédients / TM, 4 découpes + assemblage). Ensuite **1 page par recette** : badge Soir, titre, matériel, base commune en prose visuelle, vinaigrette/sauce maison dosée, déclinaisons vegan/classique, 4 pas-à-pas. Si trop long : 2e page avec « Suite · [P1] ». Ne pas miniaturiser le texte pour tout faire tenir. `jspdf` + `html2canvas`.

### Swap / Remplacement (Aujourd'hui)
- NEVER confirm a swap with a toast only. Always show a proposal sheet first.
- Step 1: user picks WHICH meal to replace (Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Dîner, Collation). Only slots that exist today and are not skipped.
- Step 2: show current meal vs proposed meal (double declination if Couple view).
- Engine: Gemini **Pro** `POST /api/generate-meals` mode **`today-swap`**. One fresh meal for **today only** (1 portion / person). Does **not** rewrite `plans_semaine`. Do **not** use mode `single` (that regenerates Lun+Mer / Mar+Jeu pairs).
- Same brain as Gem Chef: `formatKitchenPrefsForPrompt` + `formatMealCoachForPrompt` / `nutritionCoach`. Couple = **same dish**, `grams_alexis` / `grams_elodie`. Dinner low-cal; lunch/dinner `scalePlanToGoals`. No dessert in the recipe (templates already on the row).
- "Nouvelle proposition" and theme change = new Gemini call (`nonce`). Themes: Tomate, Italien, Asiatique, Bowl, Épicé, or custom. Wait overlay via `withGeminiWait`. Fallback = local catalog + user-facing warning. Never dump raw API JSON.
- Confirm persists by UPDATING the existing `repas` row (same profile + type), not inserting a duplicate.
- Lunch/dinner swap replaces the **plat** only (`withKeptDessert`): keep existing `Dessert : …` lines and their macros. Do not invent a 5th meal slot.
- Avoid list: pass `mergeAvoidTitles(pastMeals, rejected)` so a banned title is never proposed as a replacement.

### Favoris & Plus jamais (foyer)
- Same marks on **Aujourd’hui** (déjeuner / dîner with a real week recipe) **and** the Repas **recipe sheet** (`RecipeDetailSheet`): **Heart** (`FavoriteHeart`) and **Ban** (`RejectMealButton`). No marks on PD / collation / dessert-only / free-text logs.
- Heart and Ban are **exclusive** (favoriting un-bans; banning un-favorites).
- **Favoris** stores a full `PlannedMeal` snapshot (`lib/favorites.ts`). Same normalized title **updates** the snapshot. Persist `parametres.favorite_recipes` jsonb + localStorage `favorite-recipes`. Column missing → local only (`supabase/migrations/add_favorite_recipes.sql`).
- **Plus jamais** stores title + theme only (`lib/rejected.ts`). Persist `parametres.rejected_recipes` jsonb + localStorage `rejected-recipes`. Column missing → local only (`supabase/migrations/add_rejected_recipes.sql`). Ban does **not** delete the current week slot.
- Repas 4th sub-tab: segmented **Favoris | Plus jamais**. Search + group by theme. Favori sheet: edit title/theme, Retirer, **Mettre dans la semaine** → `placeRecipeInSlots` + `scalePlanToGoals` (Lun–Ven = both batch pair slots, week-end = that slot). No Gemini; no `applyTheme`. Deep retouch = place on the week then existing swap/regen, then re-heart. Plus jamais sheet: edit title/theme, add a title by hand, **Je change d’avis** removes the ban.

