## 4. TRACKING, STRAVA & LOGGING

### Screen order (Aujourd’hui, per profile)
- **Repas** (PD / déjeuner / dîner / collation) → **Faim / Énergie / Fatigue** → **Coach du jour** (only after **Validé**) → **Séance du jour** → **Activité**.
- Energy card here is `TodayEnergyCard` (eaten vs Santé). Do not reuse Métabolisme copy (Cible / Dépense estimée).

### Meal slots & skip (NO global Jeûne)
- There is NO global "Jeûne 🌙" toggle. Fasting is per meal.
- Each meal card (Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Dîner, Collation) has a discrete **Sauter / Sauté** control.
- Skipped meals: macros/calories are EXCLUDED from the daily rings; the card dims / shows a Skipped badge; tapping again restores instantly.
- Persist `repas.is_skipped`. Empty slots can be skipped by inserting a placeholder ("Repas sauté").
- Rings / daily totals always ignore `is_skipped = true`.
- Color vs `primaryGoal` (`lib/macro-status.ts`): ring, macro bars, GoalBadge, and meal kcal (vs slot share). Green = on-track or helping; red = off-goal; amber = warn. ±5% kcal = achieved.

### Desserts on Aujourd'hui (inside Déjeuner / Dîner)
- NEVER a separate dessert slot. One `repas` row per `dejeuner` / `diner`. Dessert lines are prefixed `Dessert : …` (`lib/meal-templates.ts`: `isDessertItemLine`, `splitMealItemLines`, `mergeDessertIntoMeal`).
- Cards split **Plat** vs **Dessert** (amber block). Hide a redundant title when `meal.name` is just « Déjeuner » / « Dîner ». Rings count plat + dessert kcal.
- Auto-merge Paramètres templates (`dessert-midi` → déjeuner, `dessert-soir` → dîner) even into **logged** meals if there are **no** dessert lines yet. If the user cleared dessert, persist `Dessert : —` (`isEmptyDessertMarker`) and do not re-merge.
- Dessert-only lunch/dinner is titled Déjeuner / Dîner, not the template dessert name.

### Click-to-edit meals
- Tapping a meal card opens an edit sheet: change type, ± grams, delete items, then save to `repas`.
- Changing the TYPE in that sheet RECLASSIFIES the open meal. It does NOT load another meal’s ingredients.
- Lunch/dinner sheet splits **Plat** / **Dessert**. Dessert: ± grams, delete, add via text (`Ex. Skyr 150g`). Macros: food-log estimate on dessert lines, remainder on the plat (`parseMealItems`).
- **Ajouter au plat** offers the same 3 saisie rapide modes (Texte / IA, Code-barres, Photo). Slot is already known → skip the meal-type picker; merge into the open meal **keeping dessert lines** (`appendPlatKeepingDessert`).

### Fast logging (Onglet Aujourd'hui)
- 3 modes: Text/AI, OpenFoodFacts Barcode, Vision Photo.
- MANDATORY first step for ALL three from the dashboard tiles: "À quel repas souhaitez-vous ajouter cet aliment ?" (Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Dîner, Collation). Never skip this.
- After confirm, merge into that slot: append items + macros if a meal already exists (**plat lines before dessert lines** on déjeuner/dîner); REPLACE if the slot is a skipped placeholder; INSERT if empty.
    - Text/AI: analyze first (Gemini Flash, fallback table locale `lib/food-log.ts`), then the same editable ingredient review as photo (adjust **quantity** + weight, delete / add) before save. Never write the raw AI output directly. Line format `Nom : 2 carreaux (20g)` — changing the quantity scales grams and kcal.

### Meal Photo Analysis (LLM Vision via Gemini Flash)
- Photo upload analyzes food items and estimates calories/macros.
- MANDATORY UI STEP: The app must NEVER save a photo analysis directly. It must first display an editable list of the detected ingredients and quantities.
- The user must be able to:
  1. Manually adjust the weight/quantity of each detected ingredient (e.g., + / - buttons or text input).
  2. Delete an ingredient that the AI hallucinated (trash icon).
  3. Add a missing ingredient manually (e.g., "Olive oil 10g").
- Only after this manual review will the user press "Confirm & Save".

### Barcode (OpenFoodFacts)
- After a product is recognized, the user MUST be able to change the quantity before save (they do not always eat the whole pack).
- Show serving vs pack presets (¼ / ½ / 1 portion / 1 paquet) plus ± grams / manual input.
- Scale calories and macros from the label serving. Save the chosen grams, not the default pack.

### Copy Yesterday
- NEVER copy the whole day blindly.
- Open a picker: user selects which yesterday slots to copy (Petit-déjeuner, Déjeuner, Dîner, Collation). Multi-select allowed.
- Slots with no yesterday meal are disabled. Do not copy skipped yesterday meals.
- Selected meals REPLACE today’s same profile + type (no duplicate breakfasts).

### Activity (Strava + Apple Santé)
- Section "Activité" on Aujourd'hui (not sport-only).
- Strava: list sport sessions (name, duration, kcal). Strava does NOT provide daily steps or NEAT.
- Hors sport (Apple Santé): daily steps + kcal outside sessions.
- Passive / hors-sport kcal = Apple Health active energy MINUS workout kcal already counted (Strava / Watch sessions). Never double-count the same ride/run.
- Deduplication: Prevent double-counting if Apple Watch and Strava record the same workout.

### Séance du jour (Tab 1 ← `profils.sport_routine`)
- Tab 1 reads the **logged profile’s** `sport_routine.sessions` and keeps only sessions whose `weekdays` include **today** (Europe/Paris, ISO weekday 1=Lun … 7=Dim via `lib/dates.ts` `isoWeekday`).
- Card title: **Prévu aujourd’hui** / **Séance du jour**. Show for each hit: activity, effort, duration, D+ (if cardio), exercise breakdown, Duo badge if `shared`.
- Status per session × day: **À faire** vs **Validé** (Strava). Persist validations locally (`strava-match:{profileId}:{date}`) until the real Strava webhook lands.
- Matching (placeholder + future live sync): incoming Strava activity (type mapped to Course / Vélo / Muscu / Équitation + duration) vs planned session. Match if **same activity** AND duration within **±15 min OR 25%**. On match → status Validé + Strava badge.
- Apple Santé ingest: `POST /api/webhooks/health` (alias `/api/health-webhook`) **and GET** (iOS Shortcuts often send query params). JSON / query : `steps`, `active_energy_kcal`, `resting_energy_kcal`, `distance_km`, `weight_kg`, `fat_mass_pct`, `bmi`, `workouts[]` + `profile_id` (défaut Alexis). Minutes d’exercice = somme des `duration` de `workouts` (pas de champ racine `workout_minutes`), stockées dans `logs_sante` daily (`payload.workout_minutes` + `duration_min`). `pesees` upserts poids / masse grasse / IMC. Hors sport = `active_energy_kcal` − kcal des séances dédiées (Strava / workouts).
- Dev trigger: **Simuler sync Strava** on the Today card (`lib/strava-match.ts`). Do not invent a second planned-workout source — always `profils.sport_routine`.
- Empty day: “Rien de prévu aujourd’hui” (rest). Never crash if `weekdays` is missing (treat as unscheduled).

### Renpho
- Provide UI for uploading Renpho screenshots in the "Suivi" tab, triggering OCR extraction.

